# Mainstream OS — re-run the per-card audio unmute pass whenever a new
# ALSA card appears. Catches USB hot-plug (USB headsets like Fifine,
# HyperX, Logitech that ship with PCM/Master muted), dock undock with
# audio replug, Bluetooth A2DP adapters that register a card, etc.
#
# The mainstream-audio-firstboot.service handles whatever cards were
# present at the very first boot; this rule handles every card that
# arrives later (including the same card if it gets unplugged and
# replugged during a session).
#
# Number 89 keeps this AFTER kernel/udev's own sound subsystem rules
# (50-udev-default, etc.) and BEFORE alsa-utils' 90-alsa-restore so
# our unmute pass settles before alsa-restore tries to apply saved
# state on top.
#
# `TAG+="systemd"` is REQUIRED: per systemd.device(5), SYSTEMD_WANTS=
# only takes effect on devices that are tagged "systemd" — without it
# the env var lands in the udev database but systemd-udevd never
# notifies systemd to instantiate the unit. systemd's own example
# rules in /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/99-systemd.rules pair every
# SYSTEMD_WANTS= with TAG+="systemd"; we follow suit.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="sound", KERNEL=="card[0-9]*", \
    TAG+="systemd", \
    ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="mainstream-audio-card-init@%k.service"
